From: WallView
Subject: [PATCH] Run the compositor, the tile painting workers and the DRM
 vblank observer as real-time threads

The scrolling thread and the IPC queues already run with SCHED_RR
(Thread::QOS::UserInteractive, RealTimeThreads), but the threads that
turn their work into a frame did not: ThreadedCompositor, the Skia
painting workers the compositor waits for, and WPEScreenSyncObserverDRM,
which starts every frame by delivering the display refresh to the
DisplayLink. On the NSPanel (4 cores, HZ=250, web process main thread at
100 % while scrolling a Home Assistant dashboard) they were woken up to
7 ms late, which is most of the time left before the next vblank.

WorkerPool has no QoS parameter, so the painting workers register
themselves with RealTimeThreads when they run their first task.

The vblank thread is destroyed 30 s after the display link stops and
created again on the next start; registering it with RealTimeThreads
from the UI process left it at SCHED_OTHER on the panel, so it sets
SCHED_RR itself when it starts.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/CompositingRunLoop.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/CompositingRunLoop.cpp
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@
 WTF_MAKE_TZONE_ALLOCATED_IMPL(CompositingRunLoop);
 
 CompositingRunLoop::CompositingRunLoop(Function<void ()>&& updateFunction)
-    : m_runLoop(RunLoop::create("org.webkit.ThreadedCompositor"_s, ThreadType::Graphics))
+    : m_runLoop(RunLoop::create("org.webkit.ThreadedCompositor"_s, ThreadType::Graphics, Thread::QOS::UserInteractive))
     , m_updateTimer(m_runLoop.get(), "CompositingRunLoop::UpdateTimer"_s, this, &CompositingRunLoop::updateTimerFired)
     , m_updateFunction(WTFMove(updateFunction))
